   Leineweber Ro SRL; SC Doipitici SRL},
Abstract = {Objectives: The paper aims to highlight a topic widely debated in recent
   years by many specialists in educational management and human resource
   management in the context of education reform in Romania: the university
   staff appraisal system, its impact on the quality of education and the
   limits imposed by such a procedure.
   Prior work: There is a wide theoretical and practical background in the
   human resource management literature directly related to the issues
   presented in the paper, especially concerning performance management and
   appraisal procedures used in some of the best ranked universities in the
   world.
   Approach: In order to highlight the main issues about the appraisal
   procedure used in Romanian higher education institutions, the authors of
   this paper used as a main method of research the survey. The research
   was conducted in The Bucharest Academy of Economic Studies and reveals
   the implications of performance evaluation over the overall quality of
   higher economic education.
   Results: The survey emphasises the best appraisal practices, the
   implications of evaluation over university staff performance and
   motivation.
   Implications: The overall paper and the results of the study question
   about the importance of a formalised and some times rigid evaluation
   procedure in higher education. Is this important for the academic field,
   is it necessary, is it enough to assure the quality of education?
   Originality: The paper presents and analyses the assessment procedure
   used in a Romanian university. The conducted survey highlights the
   strengths and weaknesses of such a procedure and suggests different ways
   of improvement.},
