Abstract = {A Subcomittee of the American Rheumatism Association was created to
   improve the understanding and diagnosis of osteoarthritis (OA) through
   the development of more specific criteria for diagnosis. To objectively
   determine which clinical parameters should be considered as potential
   criteria, the committee initially defined 23 historical, clinical and
   laboratory features that appeared worthy of further evaluation. The
   committee is constructing a mathematical model that may be used to
   validate the findings of the clinical studies of OA patients.},
