Number = {9},
Month = {MAY 14},
Abstract = {In a joint effort by the American Academy of Neurology, American
   Neurological Society, American Academy of Pediatrics, Child Neurology
   Society, and Society of Critical Care Medicine, a consensus on the
   determination of death by neurologic criteria for adult and pediatric
   patients was published in Neurology. The comprehensive guideline
   encompassed 85 unique recommendations on prerequisites for conducting a
   brain death examination, neurodiagnostic testing, and elements of a
   physical examination that can be undertaken to reach a diagnosis of
   death by neurologic criteria. All recommendations and the final
   guideline were agreed upon by the expert panel using a modified Delphi
   process.},
