Year = {2024},
Pages = {266-271},
Note = {1st International Conference on Social and Sustainable Innovations in
   Technology and Engineering (SASI-ITE), Tadepalligudem, INDIA, FEB 23-25,
   2024},
Organization = {IEEE Comp Soc; Campus Corp Connect; Balaji Aqua \& Poultry Feed LLP;
   Indian Bank; Code Tantra Tech Solut Pvt Ltd; Konijeti Malyadri Books
   Agencies; Kantipudi Steels; Balabadra Cloth Merchant; Nunna Lakshmi
   Narayana Paints; Yash Graph; Proton AC Engn; Deccan Traders; Spatial
   Bldg Prod; MR Traders; Sowbhagya Paper Ind; Harshini Elect Agencies;
   Sukumar Publicat; Abinandana Media; Reliance Gen Insurance; Smartech
   Printers; IEEE Vizag Bay Sect; Sasi Inst Technol \& Engn},
Abstract = {In the present computing scenario, 85\% of the data we generate every
   day is unstructured. Analyzing unstructured data from various sources to
   extract the most important information is extremely difficult.
   Furthermore, processing the same unstructured input data will take more
   time and be prone to errors. A method is proposed to restructure the
   given input to avoid problems when analyzing unstructured data. After
   restructuring, the following phase, keyword extraction, becomes crucial
   for modeling the system's requirements. Therefore, the proposed method
   is to develop an automated system for extracting keywords from text to
   achieve effective outcomes in terms of time, effort, desired output, and
   high accuracy. This paper proposes an approach based on parts of speech
   tagging to extract important parts from the document content. In
   particular, the keyword extraction technique tags the document contents
   and extracts keywords by considering the main parts of speech. It
   further identifies referenced nouns and defined verbs, along with the
   main parts of speech, to address the dependency between extracted
   keywords. After keyword extraction, the JSON format is used to organize
   structured data. The research results on various texts demonstrate that
   the proposed algorithm has higher precision, recall, and F value than
   conventional algorithms.},
