   CZECH REPUBLIC, SEP 03-07, 2012},
Organization = {Lex Comp Ltd; Masaryk Univ, Fac Informat; Univ W Bohemia, Fac Appl Sci},
Abstract = {This paper presents a method for extractive multi-document summarization
   that explores a two-phase clustering approach. First, sentences are
   clustered by similarity, and one sentence per cluster is selected, to
   reduce redundancy. Then, in order to group them according to topics,
   those sentences are clustered considering the collection of keywords
   that represent the topics in the set of texts. Evaluation reveals that
   the approach pursued produces highly informative summaries, containing
   many relevant data and no repeated information.},
