   Illinois, Grad Sch Lib \& Informat Sci, Ctr Informat Res Sci \&
   Scholarship; Univ N Carolina, Sch Informat \& Lib Sci},
Abstract = {This paper evaluates the performance of tools for the extraction of
   metadata from scientific articles. Accurate metadata extraction is an
   important task for automating the management of digital libraries. This
   comparative study is a guide for developers looking to integrate the
   most suitable and effective metadata extraction tool into their
   software. We shed light on the strengths and weaknesses of seven tools
   in common use. In our evaluation using papers from the arXiv collection,
   GROBID delivered the best results, followed by Mendeley Desktop.
   SciPlore Xtract, PDFMeat, and SVMHeaderParse also delivered good results
   depending on the metadata type to be extracted.},
